# The console of the group-model program running on the Spike functional model, filtered to
# its protocol lines; every other line dropped.  The line content itself is untouched.
#
# THE FIRST OBSERVED UART IN THIS PROTOCOL.  Until this run the 'METRIC cycles N' line and the
# MERLIN_WINDOW frame were things the harness was CHANGED to print and nothing had printed --
# firesim_batch's own docstring says of the frame "PROPOSED, NOT OBSERVED".  This is a real run
# of a real build: the program was compiled for the 71-group resnet50 capture with the vendor
# library and the riscv64-unknown-elf toolchain, and these are the bytes it emitted.
#
#   elf_sha256          220f2296c45790d36747e02cea9475299c293cac7fbd6e77b9dba1a603cc5547
#   program_sha256      77eb79ffb4ed2fde005922a3065e1c86204e2d8972161d5e19e5927b8c2399e2
#   window_label        group_model
#   device_groups       71 of 72
#   capture             out/artifacts/recaptures/resnet50_sum_and_mean_20260917
#
# All 71 of its group checksums equal the oracle in
# merlin/contract/firesim_uart_policies/resnet50_group_model_cycle_claim_v2.json, as do seven
# real FPGA runs -- so the emission change did not disturb what the program computes.
#
# WHAT THIS IS NOT: a hardware measurement.  Spike is a FUNCTIONAL model; its 'METRIC cycles'
# value is an instruction count, not a cycle count from the device, and no performance claim may
# cite it.  What it establishes is the PROTOCOL: that a build of this harness emits lines the
# receipt parser accepts, framed around the numbers a v2 policy declares.
